  "text": "Use this skillNobody has reviewed this skill. It passed automated structural and signature checks, which can only ever reject — a pass is not a statement that it is safe. Read the source on GitHub before you run it, particularly anything under scripts/.Download the skill (5.6 KB)A zip of this folder. Upload it wherever your agent tool takes skills — no git, no command line.Add the marketplace, once/plugin marketplace add AI-Lab-for-Cities-at-Harvard/civic-skill-exchangeCopyInstall it/plugin install ns-example-skill@civic-skill-exchangeCopyJust this skillnpx degit AI-Lab-for-Cities-at-Harvard/civic-skill-exchange/skills/ns/example-skill example-skillCopyThe whole registrygit clone https://github.com/AI-Lab-for-Cities-at-Harvard/civic-skill-exchange.gitCopyIn Claude Code the two /plugin lines are all you need. Skills here follow the open Agent Skills format, so they also work in ChatGPT, Codex, Gemini CLI, Copilot, Cursor and others — those take a skill at a time, so use the download above.Install paths differ across agent tools — .claude/skills/, .agents/skills/, and others. Check your tool's docs for where it looks.View on GitHub →",
}
`;

